<h1>View group details</h1>
<p class="lead">
  Open a separate window to read a study group's meeting information.
</p>

<h2>Before you begin</h2>
<p>
  You need at least one group in the current session.
  If the list is empty, <a href="/features/create-group">create a group</a>
  and click <strong>Show all</strong>.
</p>

<h2>Step-by-step instructions</h2>
<ol>
  <li>Find a group in the main window by
      <a href="/features/browse-groups">browsing groups</a>
      or <a href="/features/search">searching by course code</a>.</li>
  <li>Click the group in the list to select it.</li>
  <li>Click <strong>View details</strong>.</li>
  <li>In the separate details window, review the group name,
      course, description, meeting time, location,
      and <strong>Maximum members</strong>.</li>
  <li>Click <strong>Close</strong> to return to the main window.</li>
</ol>

<figure>
  <img src="/images/studyhub-details.png"
       alt="StudyHub details window showing the CS101 Study Crew group's meeting information">
  <figcaption>
    The details window displays the information entered when the group
    was created.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<h2>What to expect</h2>
<p>
  The details window is read-only. Viewing or closing it does not change
  the group. You must select a group before opening its details.
</p>

<aside class="notice">
  <strong>Understanding the information:</strong>
  Maximum members is the group's configured capacity, not a count of
  enrolled members. Meeting time is descriptive text; StudyHub does not
  schedule events or check for time conflicts.
</aside>

<p>
  Next: <a href="/features/search">Search by course code</a>
</p>

